WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.331 --> 00:00:03.831
(gentle electronic music)

00:00:05.115 --> 00:00:06.370
- [Faith] When you highline often,

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:10.962
you really learn to train
your fear like a muscle.

00:00:10.962 --> 00:00:13.833
Sometimes the height
isn't the scariest part.

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:15.899
Sometimes it's the exposure,

00:00:15.899 --> 00:00:19.098
which is how much space you
can perceive around you.

00:00:19.098 --> 00:00:22.598
(gentle electronic music)

00:00:25.239 --> 00:00:26.465
My name is Faith Dickey,

00:00:26.465 --> 00:00:29.935
and I'm a professional slackliner.

00:00:29.935 --> 00:00:33.494
(gentle instrumental music)

00:00:33.494 --> 00:00:35.269
So slacklining is the umbrella term

00:00:35.269 --> 00:00:37.224
for all the different facets of walking

00:00:37.224 --> 00:00:39.639
on a flat, woven band.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.829
One of these facets is highlining,

00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:46.239
which is walking a slack
line high off the ground.

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:48.615
One of the best ways
to train for highlining

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:51.353
is setting up slack lines over water.

00:00:51.353 --> 00:00:53.357
When the current is
passing underneath you,

00:00:53.357 --> 00:00:56.739
you automatically start to
fall that same direction,

00:00:56.739 --> 00:00:59.999
and it's almost like you're
not in control of your body,

00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:02.084
and that's great practice for highlining

00:01:02.084 --> 00:01:03.568
because in highlining when you're dealing

00:01:03.568 --> 00:01:05.533
with all the fear and adrenaline,

00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:07.626
oftentimes it feels like
you're not in control

00:01:07.626 --> 00:01:09.558
of your own body either.

00:01:09.558 --> 00:01:10.966
(water splashing)

00:01:10.966 --> 00:01:14.672
(gentle electronic music)

00:01:14.672 --> 00:01:18.884
Chamonix is a town in the Alps of France,

00:01:18.884 --> 00:01:20.001
and it's one of the places

00:01:20.001 --> 00:01:22.498
that really drives me in highlining.

00:01:22.498 --> 00:01:24.329
What's different about
highlining in the Alps

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:27.987
is that the whole
experience is more intense.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.739
Being that high off the ground,

00:01:29.739 --> 00:01:31.069
you look at the valley below,

00:01:31.069 --> 00:01:33.464
and the houses are just tiny specks.

00:01:33.464 --> 00:01:34.822
They look like toys.

00:01:34.822 --> 00:01:36.322
It's unbelievable.

00:01:38.091 --> 00:01:40.717
One of the highlines that I
walked recently in Chamonix

00:01:40.717 --> 00:01:42.562
was on Aiguille du Midi,

00:01:42.562 --> 00:01:43.845
and when we reached the top,

00:01:43.845 --> 00:01:46.363
it was a totally clear, blue sky,

00:01:46.363 --> 00:01:48.344
and we were surrounded by peaks,

00:01:48.344 --> 00:01:49.835
but during the process of rigging,

00:01:49.835 --> 00:01:52.266
the clouds started to roll in.

00:01:52.266 --> 00:01:55.715
It was like an acid trip walking the line.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.745
I was out there in space and exposure,

00:01:57.745 --> 00:01:58.769
trying to balance,

00:01:58.769 --> 00:02:00.971
and the line was swinging beneath me.

00:02:00.971 --> 00:02:03.520
Meanwhile, these huge,
white clouds were passing,

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.957
and the line would disappear.

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:06.324
The anchor would disappear,

00:02:06.324 --> 00:02:08.257
and then it would reappear,

00:02:08.257 --> 00:02:09.866
and there was no way to control it.

00:02:09.866 --> 00:02:11.699
I just had to hang on.

00:02:12.714 --> 00:02:14.864
- [Woman] Yes. (murmuring)

00:02:14.864 --> 00:02:15.697
Oh man.

00:02:15.697 --> 00:02:17.322
- [Faith] The beauty of
the mountains is awesome,

00:02:17.322 --> 00:02:21.392
and yet it is a landscape that
demands focus and respect.

00:02:21.392 --> 00:02:24.023
Alpine highlining is the
purest form of the sport

00:02:24.023 --> 00:02:25.311
I can think of.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:28.894
(gentle electronic music)

